In order to estimate the parameters for the model in Fig. 1, we simultaneously fit to both steady state and time-course data to capture the redundancy in parameters between data types. We undertake an approach that allows us to generate full parameter probability distributions, as opposed to a single best fit parameter set. Additionally, we incorporate expected values for a given parameter through setting a prior distribution as opposed to single literature-based values, allowing the results to reflect known quantitation for RTK mechanisms without constraining the result to any single RTK or condition. These goals are achieved using Bayes Theorem,6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
